// - Reserve only 100 steps for the constrained span (avg answer is ~5-10 tokens)
// - Use 800 steps for reasoning to give the model context
// - Use hard ConstrainedStep throughout the span
// - Add an aggressive completeness check every step
// - If budget runs out, force close at any complete prefix
//
// Actually looking more carefully: "avg 47.88 tokens" with maxSteps=900 means
// the strategy is terminating EXTREMELY early - only using ~48 of 900 steps!
// This happens because UnconstrainedChunk stops when stoppedOnEos or when
// "<<" is observed. The model is emitting EOS very early in the reasoning.
//
// ROOT CAUSE: The model emits "<<" in its chain-of-thought reasoning (like
// "the answer is <<"), UnconstrainedChunk stops there, we enter the constrained
// span... but we're mid-sentence and have very few steps left because the
// reasoning chunk counted stepsUsed. Then we run ConstrainedStep but it returns
// EOS immediately because the model wants to finish the sequence.
//
// REAL FIX:
// 1. Don't use UnconstrainedChunk at all - use step-by-step UnconstrainedStep
//    to suppress "<<" properly
// 2. OR: Force-stop reasoning at a FIXED budget (e.g., 800 steps), ignoring
//    whether "<<" was seen
// 3. Then ALWAYS force a fresh span
//
// With avg 47.88 tokens and SPAN_RESERVE=300:
// - reasoningBudget = 900 - 300 = 600
// - But UnconstrainedChunk stops at "<<" after ~25 tokens
// - Then constrained loop starts but model outputs EOS
//
// Solution: After reasoning stops (regardless of why), ALWAYS force open a new
// span if not inside one already. The constrained prompt should provide enough
// context for the model to generate the correct expression.
//
// Additionally: Use a guidance string to tell the model to output the numeric
